  "limitations": [
    "The dissimilarities between our experimental situation and the urban environment limit the generality of our findings to macro crowding phenomena.",
    "Subjects in our study, unlike the inhabitants of a crowded city, experience crowding for a relatively short period of time and realize that they will eventually leave the situation.",
    "The lack of such effects (on task performance, enjoyment, relatedness, liking, hostility) may be attributable to the consistently high level of game enjoyment expressed by subjects in all conditions.",
    "The potency of the room size manipulation may have 'swamped out' the effect of a competitive task set on the perception of crowding within the small room.",
    "The subjects' physical discomfort, despite our attempt to control it, made the differential effect of task set on perceived crowding, within the small and large rooms, even more unlikely.",
    "Since this experiment did not control for or manipulate the factor of time, it is impossible to ascertain whether the perception of crowding actually decreased over time within the small room, competitive condition.",
    "The suggestion that different connotations of spatial limitation for males and females may lead to different attributions of crowding feelings is highly speculative and remains to be investigated empirically.",
    "It was impossible to ascertain whether the increased level of laughter and noise perceived in the small room, competitive condition reflected the absence of crowding, a mode of coping with it, or even a nonspatial source of heightened crowding.",
    "Experimenter effects (on perceived quietness of the room, name recall, and number of jokes) are neither uniquely relevant for understanding crowding nor easily interpretable."
  ],
